"xin chào": {"etymology":[{"vi":"xin"}," (“to ask for”) + ",{"vi":"chào"}," (“to greet”). This appears to be a modern coinage, as it is not attested in pre-modern documents."],"pos":[{"name":"Verb","senses":[{"gloss":["to cordially greet"],"labels":["informal","polite"],"examples":[{"vi":"(Chúng tôi) xin (kính) chào quý vị và các bạn.","en":"We'd like to cordially welcome you to our establishment."}]}]}],"usage_notes":[["This is rather artificial as a greeting and often used as a direct translation of English hello. Also very common in interface labels."],["In formal contexts, ",{"vi":"kính chào"}," is used instead. For a softer and more polite tone, ",{"vi":"xin kính chào"}," is often used, particularly by newsreaders and television hosts."],["For everyday greetings, ",{"vi":"chào"}," followed by a kinship term is used. In close relationships and casual communication, ",{"vi":"hế lô"}," is also used, especially among Millennial and younger speakers."],["For phone calls, ",{"vi":"a-lô"}," is the default greeting."]]},
